❑Recall that you use: Math.methodName(arguments);

to invoke a method in the Math class.
Example: Math.pow(3, 2.5); 
❑Can you invoke getArea() using Circle.getArea()?
The answer is no. All the methods used in Math are static, 
which are defined using the static keyword.
❑However, getArea() is non-static. It must be invoked from 
an object using: objectRefVar.getArea(arguments);
